# OffLoad Laundry Landing Page - Environment Variables
#
# APPS_SCRIPT_ENDPOINT
# The Google Apps Script Web App URL that receives lead form submissions
# and writes them to Google Sheets.
#
# IMPORTANT: This variable does NOT use the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix, which means
# it is only accessible server-side (in Route Handlers, Server Components, etc.)
# and is never exposed to the browser/client bundle. (Req 12.4, 12.5)
#
# Setup steps:
# 1. Create a new Google Sheet with header row: Timestamp | Full Name | Instagram Username
# 2. Open Extensions > Apps Script and paste the code from apps-script/Code.gs
# 3. Deploy as a Web App:
#    - Execute as: Me
#    - Who has access: Anyone
# 4. Copy the deployment URL (ends with /exec)
# 5. Paste it below in your .env.local file (do NOT commit .env.local)
# 6. Restart the dev server after setting the variable

APPS_SCRIPT_ENDPOINT=
